\newlabel{fig_main_method}{{1}{2}{Our ParaDis method is based on the classic genetic zero-cost framework. Any ZCP can be used in the role of the explorer and select architectures that go on to reproduction. The ParaDis discriminator discards architectures based on parameter count distribution statistics over the population, with the size of architectures sampled at each generation controlled by $\tau $}{figure.caption.1}{}}
